<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tacna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Alto de la Alianza · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacna">Tacna</a>, or of the Alto de la Alianza, was fought on 26 May 1880 near Tacna in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a>. The Chilean army defeated the allied Peruvian and Bolivian forces commanded by the Bolivian president Narciso Campero. After the defeat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> withdrew its army from the war, leaving Peru to fight on alone, and Chile kept control of the coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tacna.jpg" alt="Battle of Tacna" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlos Prieto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla-de-tacna.djvu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
